      "agentRuntime": "langgraph",
      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here's how **long rests** work in Frosthaven:\n\n## Declaring a Long Rest\n\nDuring the **Card Selection** step, instead of playing two cards, a character may declare a long rest — provided they have **at least two cards in their discard pile**. A long rest constitutes their **entire turn for the round** and is performed on **initiative 99**.\n\n## Long Rest Steps\n\nWhen a character long rests, they follow these steps in order:\n\n1. **Lose one card of their choice** from their discard pile, then return all remaining discarded cards to their hand. *(mandatory)*\n2. **Perform \"*Heal* 2, self\"** *(optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items** *(optional)* — items can even be used during the same turn they are recovered.\n\n> \"When a character long rests, they lose one card of their choice from their discard pile and return the remaining cards to their hand (mandatory). Perform 'Heal 2, self' (optional). Recover all of their spent items (optional). Items can be used during the same turn in which they are recovered.\"\n\n*(Frosthaven Rulebook, p. 38)*",
